thread:
alex: Quick check — I'm planning a Terraform change to move per-model runtime flags out of the central ConfigMap and into per-deployment annotations to reduce hot-reload storms. Will open PR shortly. Anyone running workloads that expect live ConfigMap updates for feature flags?

sam: @alex please drop the TF diff here when ready — main worry is the model runtime that listens for ConfigMap changes to invalidate KV cache. Will that still work?

alex: short diff: ```resource "kubernetes_deployment" "model" {
  metadata {
    annotations = {
      "model.redwood/runtime-flags" = jsonencode(var.runtime_flags)
    }
  }
}
# removing data from ConfigMap and switching to annotation-based flags``` It's a shim: an init sidecar reads annotation on deploy and writes to local file for the model process. No in-cluster ConfigMap watcher anymore.

nina: hmm sidecar approach ok, but how do we update flags at runtime without rollout? We rely on live toggles for perf experiments.

mike: If we remove ConfigMap, you lose kube-propagated updates. Could we keep ConfigMap for ops toggles and use annotations for deploy-bound knobs? Also what's the polling/TTL behaviour of the sidecar?

alex: plan: two-tier — annotations for deploy-time knobs (quant profile, thread pool sizes, GC knobs), ConfigMap kept for ops toggles (feature flags) with a lightweight controller that only triggers for keys in ops namespace. Sidecar polls annotation only on start; controller watches ConfigMap and posts a webhook to the sidecar for live changes. Will document.

lisa: small nit: ensure TF state migration — old configmap.data -> annotations? Add a migration job to copy values into new "model.redwood/runtime-flags" annotation on deployments. Otherwise a rollout may drop flags.

alex: good call. I'll add a k8s Job in the PR to patch deployments to add annotation from existing ConfigMap. Also will add a TF var `keep_configmap = true` for staged migration.

deploy-bot: Deployment patch job queued: staging/runtime-flags-migrate-2026-03-17

sam: thanks — pls tag eng-runtime and eng-ml on the PR, and add a short runbook for rollback (recreate ConfigMap if migration goes wrong).

alex: Will do. PR in ~20m. Thanks all :thumbsup:
